Thanks all for the helpful responses. Some of my thoughts along with
some more questions...

My starting horse got killed early on and I ended up going steedless up
to Medusa, mainly out of laziness but also because I lacked a
stethoscope, magic whistle, or healing spell. In retrospect, I think
that was probably a bad idea - it seems to me that the early to mid-game
is where the lance should really shine. I had held off using it because
I didn't want it to break on me (this depends somewhat on Luck from what
I've read?), but that's really kind of pointless - by the time you hit
Medusa, you should have a decent artifact weapon and maybe enough armor
to twoweapon, and then you'd drop the lance anyway. I also didn't
realize until recently just how easy it is to level up a steed once you
get yourself halfway established. In any event, I got one early wish
(SDSM) and got Grayswandir from a sac (my only gift in ~100 sacrifices,
but at least it's a good one) so I was in pretty strong shape
regardless.

As for the steed, Puff the Magic Green Dragon got himself killed by a
death ray in Ludios before I had a /oUT and then I flirted briefly with
a Silver Dragon before deciding they were just too slow by that point. I
was fortunate enough to find a +oChM and finally a magic whistle around
the Castle, but I've yet to see a Ki-rin cross my path. So for the
moment I've got a Jabberwock, which has worked fine through the first
half of Gehennom. It's 4/3 speed (after /oSM) and killer attacks lead me
to think it should carry me up to the Planes without much problem.
Doesn't look I'll be seeing any Ki-rin at this point unless I get lucky
with Create Monster (they don't spawn in Gehennom, right?), so I'm
prepared to hoof it out on foot at the end.

Answer me these questions three...

1) If you levitate on a non-flying steed, will the steed levitate with
you? It works fine on the flyers, which surprised me, but I haven't
thought about non-flyers until just now.

2) Are Ki-rin "intelligent"? That is, would they wear an "oR or drink
!oGL if I provided them to it? I'm assuming they don't wear armor, being
vaguely horsey creatures. I'm trying to decide whether a figurine would
be worth my last wish over the extra 4-5 AC from a Hawaiian shirt I've
yet to find (no poly-piling). I've got -29 at the moment, which I can
only get down to -33 to -35 (without a Shirt) after writing scrolls, due
to continued crappy luck enchanting and praying for protection. In my
last two ascensions, I really appreciated a better than -40 AC and I'm a
little leary of hitting the Planes above -35.

3) (Not Knight related) Is the priest of Moloch in the Valley guaranteed
to have a robe? I burned Castle wishes on a robe with both my Wizard and
my Knight, thinking I'd never see one otherwise. When my Jabberwock iced
the priest and I saw the robe, I realized that I had seen it there in
the Wizard game as well. D'oh!

